{"baseRefName":"main","baseRefOid":"98585733518b6188650c5c4818d26582fd0d1a0a","body":"Closes #715.\n\n## Problem\n\nUnder the #666 F07 policy, a simple TrueType font with the Symbolic flag, no `/Encoding` and no `/ToUnicode` maps every code to U+FFFD. Office exports post-processed by Ghostscript routinely emit ordinary Latin subset fonts in exactly this shape:\n\n- (3,0) cmap at `0xF020–0xF0FF`, plus a (1,0) cmap\n- `post` format 3\n\nWhole pages therefore extract as replacement characters, and no error is reported.\n\n## Change\n\nThis adds `TextExtractor::with_symbolic_truetype_fallback(bool)`, which is **off by default**, so the existing contract and output are unchanged unless a caller opts in.\n\nWhen enabled, for symbolic simple TrueType fonts with no `/Encoding`:\n\n1. Each code resolves to a glyph through the embedded `FontFile2`, following ISO 32000-1 §9.6.6.4:\n   - the (3,0) subtable at `code`, or at `0xF000`, `0xF100` or `0xF200` + `code`;\n   - otherwise the (1,0) subtable at `code`.\n2. If the glyph's `post` name has a Unicode assignment, that name is used.\n3. If the glyph has no `post` name (format 3, typical for subsets), the code decodes as its WinAnsiEncoding character when found via (3,0), or its MacRomanEncoding character when found via (1,0).\n4. The following still yield U+FFFD:\n   - codes the program does not map;\n   - glyphs whose `post` name has no Unicode assignment;\n   - fonts without a parseable embedded program.\n5. `/ToUnicode` and valid `/Differences` names keep precedence. Codes that a `/ToUnicode` CMap omits are **not** filled from the program.\n\nIt also adds `TrueTypeFont::post_glyph_names()` (`pub(crate)`), which reads `post` formats 1.0 and 2.0. Truncated name data is handled without panicking.\n\n## Tests\n\n- **`tests/text_symbolic_truetype_fallback_test.rs`** (new) reuses the #666 symbolic fixtures. Their `post` tables swap the names for `A` and `B`, which proves that `post` names take precedence over the byte. The tests cover:\n  - the default and explicitly-disabled strict behaviour;\n  - byte fallback via (3,0)/WinAnsi and via (1,0)/MacRoman;\n  - `post` name precedence;\n  - unmapped codes;\n  - ToUnicode and Differences precedence;\n  - an unparseable program.\n- **Unit tests for `post` parsing** cover formats 1.0, 2.0 (standard and custom names), truncation, 3.0 and a missing table.\n- **Existing contract suites** still pass unchanged: `text_symbolic_truetype_contract_test`, `text_competing_cmap_contract_test` and `text_output_api_contract_test`.\n\n## Real-world validation\n\nI tested on a ~1,700-page Office→Ghostscript document. The content is not included because it contains personal data.\n\n| | U+FFFD chars | pages >50% U+FFFD |\n|---|---|---|\n| 5.2.0 | 12 | 0 |\n| 5.4.2 (default / flag off) | 1,894,630 | 946 |\n| this PR, flag on | 95,938 | 43 |\n\n- With the flag off, the output is byte-identical to 5.4.1.\n- With the flag on, the affected pages match 5.2.0's text.\n- The remaining U+FFFD come from an unrelated Type3 font with numeric glyph names. 5.2.0 does not produce real text for those pages either.\n\n## Note\n\n`cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings` currently fails on `tests/annotations_comprehensive_test.rs` (`for_kv_map`) on `main`, independently of this change. Clippy is clean for the library and the new test target.\n","commits":[{"authoredDate":"2026-10-12T10:11:08Z","authors":[{"email":"oshtivi@paloaltonetworks.com","id":"U_kgDOC1kNhA","login":"oshtivi","name":"Omer Shtivi"}],"committedDate":"2026-10-12T10:11:08Z","messageBody":"Symbolic simple TrueType fonts without /Encoding or /ToUnicode map every\ncode to U+FFFD under the #666 F07 policy. Office exports post-processed by\nGhostscript routinely mark ordinary Latin subset fonts this way, so whole\npages extract as replacement characters.\n\nAdd TextExtractor::with_symbolic_truetype_fallback (off by default). When\nenabled, each code resolves to a glyph through the embedded FontFile2 (3,0)\nsubtable (code, 0xF000/0xF100/0xF200 + code) or (1,0) subtable per\nISO 32000-1 9.6.6.4. The glyph's post name is used when it has a Unicode\nassignment; unnamed glyphs fall back to the byte's WinAnsi (via 3,0) or\nMacRoman (via 1,0) character. Unmapped codes, glyphs named without a\nUnicode assignment, and fonts without a parseable program stay U+FFFD.\nToUnicode and valid Differences names keep precedence.\n\nAdd TrueTypeFont::post_glyph_names for post formats 1.0 and 2.0.\n\nCloses #715","messageHeadline":"fix(text): opt-in symbolic TrueType decoding via embedded program (#715)","oid":"cfcf0fd3d4ec3631cc39f98fea9afbd371e88ca2"},{"authoredDate":"2026-10-12T11:12:49Z","authors":[{"email":"oshtivi@paloaltonetworks.com","id":"U_kgDOC1kNhA","login":"oshtivi","name":"Omer Shtivi"}],"committedDate":"2026-10-12T11:12:49Z","messageBody":"","messageHeadline":"style: order TrueTypeFont import for rustfmt","oid":"7b6839f04499b6c5b9155a398bee96e327da5ab6"}],"files":[{"path":"oxidize-pdf-core/src/text/extraction.rs","additions":38,"deletions":2},{"path":"oxidize-pdf-core/src/text/extraction_cmap.rs","additions":93,"deletions":2},{"path":"oxidize-pdf-core/src/text/fonts/truetype.rs","additions":154,"deletions":1},{"path":"oxidize-pdf-core/tests/text_symbolic_truetype_fallback_test.rs","additions":144,"deletions":0}],"headRefName":"fix/issue-715-symbolic-truetype-fallback","headRefOid":"7b6839f04499b6c5b9155a398bee96e327da5ab6","mergeStateStatus":"CLEAN","mergeable":"MERGEABLE","number":716,"statusCheckRollup":[{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-10-12T11:27:29Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/bzsanti/oxidizePdf/actions/runs/38241226841/job/114784049540","name":"Test (ubuntu-latest, stable)","startedAt":"2026-10-12T11:13:05Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"CI"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-10-12T11:17:14Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/bzsanti/oxidizePdf/actions/runs/38241226790/job/114784049204","name":"T0 +